# .privacy-allow — synthetic / intentional values this repo contains, declared
# as literal VALUES (one per line) so the guard stops flagging them. COMMITTED.
# See .privacy-allow.example for the full format notes.

# The bundled ws_mount pattern matches the workspace's own mount paths, which
# appear in committed docs/configs as the project path. Generic, deprecated
# mount points (standardized to ~/Projects on 2026-06-11), not device
# identifiers. Scoped to the exact literals so a genuinely sensitive mount
# (e.g. /media/sf_*) still fires.
/mnt/Projects
/mnt/shared

# The GitHub SSH user@host trips the email regex but is a public, non-identifying
# value — it appears in clone-URL examples in deploy docs. Current source now uses
# the HTTPS clone URL (correct for a public repo's audience); this literal remains
# in older history, and a filter-repo rewrite would be absurd for a benign host
# string. Declared known-safe rather than scrubbed.
git@github.com
